  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/07-carp-like-fishes-1-loaches/yasuhikotakia_lecontei_en/",
      "html": "<p>This loach originates from the Mekong watershed and reaches a length of about 15 cm. The name red finned loach is somewhat misleading, since not all animals show this colouring at all stages of age. During development they change colours and pattern. Young animals usually exhibit a pattern of stripes which disappears with age.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/07-carp-like-fishes-1-loaches/yasuhikotakia_lecontei_en/",
      "html": "<p>Thailand, Vietnam, Mekong.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "habitat",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/07-carp-like-fishes-1-loaches/yasuhikotakia_lecontei_en/",
      "html": "<p>In their homeland they inhabit running waters with a stony ground.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "aquariumSize",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/07-carp-like-fishes-1-loaches/yasuhikotakia_lecontei_en/",
      "html": "<p>Since they are very active swimmers, the aquarium should have a length of at least 1 m.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "maintenance",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/07-carp-like-fishes-1-loaches/yasuhikotakia_lecontei_en/",
      "html": "<p>Y. lecontei (formerly known as Botia lecontei) is predominantly active at dawn and at night, so sharp light should be avoided.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/07-carp-like-fishes-1-loaches/yasuhikotakia_lecontei_en/",
      "html": "<p>The food should contain mostly meaty components; snails are a favoured delicacy.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/07-carp-like-fishes-1-loaches/yasuhikotakia_lecontei_en/",
      "html": "<p>No information is available about natural reproduction in captivity. As with the majority of loaches, it has probably not yet occurred.</p>"
    }
  ],
